  "id": "Compound::DB00321 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Amitriptyline exhibits a consistent interaction with Cyp2d6 through multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role in modulating its activity. The evidence indicates that Amitriptyline binds to Cyp2e1, which is involved in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid. This process is further mediated by Cyp2d6, which participates in the same metabolic pathway. The overlapping roles of Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6 in arachidonic acid metabolism suggest a shared functional context, potentially explaining the observed interactions. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores supports a robust mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Cyp2e1 in linking Amitriptyline to Cyp2d6, emphasizing the role of enzyme activity in drug-target interactions.",
